{"causes": ["The societal norm of royal illegitimacy allowed Maurice de Saxe to be acknowledged and provided with opportunities despite his birth.", "The fragmented political landscape of 18th-century Europe, characterized by dynastic rivalries, provided ample opportunities for talented military commanders.", "His early military training under Prince Eugene of Savoy exposed him to advanced tactical and strategic thinking from a young age."], "effects": ["Maurice de Saxe's victories significantly contributed to France's territorial gains and strategic position at the Treaty of Aix-la-Chapelle in 1748.", "His treatise 'Mes Rêveries sur l'Art de la Guerre' became a canonical text, influencing military theory and practice for generations of European commanders.", "Saxe's innovative tactical approaches, particularly at Fontenoy, demonstrated the effectiveness of combined arms and flexible formations, leading to shifts in battlefield doctrine."], "relationships": [{"sourceSlug": "maurice-de-saxe", "sourceName": "Maurice de Saxe", "verb": "PARTICIPATES_IN", "targetSlug": "war-of-the-austrian-succession", "targetName": "War of the Austrian Succession", "context": "Maurice de Saxe served as a key French commander during the War of the Austrian Succession (1740–1748), achieving decisive victories."}, {"sourceSlug": "augustus-ii-the-strong", "sourceName": "Augustus II the Strong", "verb": "INFLUENCES", "targetSlug": "maurice-de-saxe", "targetName": "Maurice de Saxe", "context": "Maurice de Saxe's noble birth as the illegitimate son of Augustus II the Strong provided him with status and early military opportunities."}, {"sourceSlug": "maurice-de-saxe", "sourceName": "Maurice de Saxe", "verb": "CREATES", "targetSlug": "mes-reveries-sur-lart-de-la-guerre", "targetName": "Mes Rêveries sur l'Art de la Guerre", "context": "Maurice de Saxe authored 'Mes Rêveries sur l'Art de la Guerre', a posthumously published military treatise influencing future generations."}, {"sourceSlug": "maur